1. MIT DB Lab Dataset

This dataset was collected by the MIT Database Group to study human activity and environmental sensing in a laboratory setting.
It includes:

Sensor readings from various environmental sensors (e.g., temperature, humidity, light, sound).

Data related to human presence, movement, and lab usage patterns.

Use Cases:
Useful for research in context-aware systems, activity recognition, and IoT data analysis.

Source: MIT Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Laboratory (CSAIL)
Link: https://db.csail.mit.edu/labdata/labdata.html

License: Refer to the dataset page for licensing and usage terms.

2. Zenodo Smart Building Sensor Dataset

This dataset contains real-world sensor data collected from a smart building environment.
It includes:

Measurements such as temperature, humidity, light intensity, and CO₂ concentration.

Time-series data from multiple sensors deployed in office spaces.

Use Cases:
Ideal for time-series forecasting, anomaly detection, and energy efficiency research.

Source: Zenodo Open Research Data Repository
Link: https://zenodo.org/records/2654726

License: Open-access (see dataset record for specific license details).
